      {
        "index0Based": 91,
        "exactText": "events, skaters cover 16 laps of the oval. As the name implies, all competitors are on the ice at one time. During the race there are three intermediate sprints (after four, eight and 12 laps) for which skaters are awarded points (three for first, two for second, one for third) that count towards the final standings. The final sprint to the finish awards 60 points for first, 40 points for second, and 20 points for third, ensuring that the first three skaters to complete the 16 laps are also ranked as the top three in the race results.",
        "SHA256": "e518a3fd94fc773a2039ed4cf956eeab16dd336b4a2c5752ccbdc7977a86ecb4"
